From 9a7dd942a90b9d57e4db86292b323900819e0ada Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Kimathi <kimathi@example.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 17:56:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve merge conflict between old core app and new modular
 apps

- Remove apps.core (Faculty, Department, Program, Room, Lecturer,
  ValidStaffID) in favor of the new modular apps.departments,
  apps.lecturers, apps.programs, apps.rooms
- Move ValidStaffID into apps.accounts (its only real consumer)
- Redirect all apps.core imports (mapper.py, notifications, accounts
  auth_views.py) to the new modular apps
- Wire departments/programs/rooms/lecturers/units/students/enrollments
  urls into config/urls.py (previously only reachable via apps.core)
- Remove dead duplicate files shadowed by same-named packages
  (accounts/{models,serializers,views}.py, timetable/{models,
  serializers,views}.py, students/urls/urls.py)
- Fix TimetableSlotAdmin referencing removed 'day' field -> day_of_week
- Fix StudentUnit.unit FK to point at units.Unit instead of removed
  timetable.Unit
- Clean up duplicated router blocks in departments/programs/units urls.py
- Reset and regenerate all migrations project-wide, since old core-era
  migration history no longer matched current models (test data only,
  confirmed safe to reset)

Verified: manage.py check passes clean, full migrate applies
end-to-end against a fresh database.
